module

public import CORALean.ContSet.Ellipsoid.Real.Theorems.ConstructEqSqrt
public import CORALean.ContSet.Ellipsoid.Real.Operations.Mtimes
public import CORALean.ContSet.Ellipsoid.Real.Theorems.ConstructEqOfFactor
public import CORALean.ContSet.Ellipsoid.Real.Theorems.MulGMulTranspose

@[expose] public section

/-!
# A linear image of an ellipsoid is exactly an ellipsoid

[1, Lemma 2], `T E(E, ē) = E(T E Tᵀ, T ē)`, for every `T`, singular ones included. `M G` is a
factor of `M Q Mᵀ` (`G` the square root of `Q`), so the image is generated by it
(`construct_eq_of_factor`), and then the same unit-ball point works in both directions — a
matrix in front of `G` introduces no freedom and removes none — and associativity of `M (G u)` is
the whole proof.

## References

* [1] V. Gaßmann and M. Althoff. "Scalable Zonotope-Ellipsoid Conversions using the Euclidean
      Zonotope Norm". In Proc. of the 2020 American Control Conference (ACC), pp. 4715-4721,
      2020.
-/

